 ## Overview
-Point-based Isosurface Extraction with Octree Pruning is a view-dependent surface extraction method that recursively subdivides a scalar field into grid cells until sub-pixel resolution is achieved in screen space, rendering the resulting geometry using point primitives [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods by combining adaptive spatial decomposition with visibility-based pruning to handle large unstructured grids interactively on GPUs, rather than generating a static mesh [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+Point-based Isosurface Extraction with Octree Pruning is a view-dependent surface extraction method that recursively subdivides a scalar field into grid cells until sub-pixel resolution is achieved in screen space, rendering the resulting geometry using point primitives [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [Standard Interval Tree for Isosurface Extraction](1230-standard-interval-tree-for-isosurface-extraction.md) and [IsoOctree](1744-isooctree.md) by combining adaptive spatial decomposition with visibility-based pruning to handle large unstructured grids interactively on GPUs, rather than generating a static mesh [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs**
